From 4839931247cc8910e1edcfb69ad18ebef544e3a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mika Laitio <mika.laitio@amd.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 20:46:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Add ROCm W4A8 INT8 fallback and
 native kernels

INT4-weight and dynamic INT8-activation checkpoints
could not run on ROCm. The first ROCm W4A8 path used
a dequant fallback.

Reason:
- W4A8 INT8 MoE exposed only a CPU backend.
- Dense ROCm kernels require biased uint4 packing.
- SM90 W4A8 detection ignored activation type.
- Unpacked INT4 checkpoints exceeded gfx1201 memory.
- Fallback dequant wasted ROCm INT8 matrix cores.

Fix:
- Distinguish INT8 and FP8 W4A8 activation formats.
- The interim path quantized and dequantized per token.
- Reuse packed W4A16 Triton dense and MoE kernels.
- Support unpacked and post-packed checkpoints.
- Preserve packed weights through model loading.
- Add native INT8xINT4 GEMM and dynamic quantization.
- Plumb INT8 scales through MoE Triton expert kernels.
- Extend tests for GEMM accuracy and W4A8 routing.

Testing
- Pass seven W4A8 routing and packing tests.
- Pass 14 Triton INT4 GEMM cases on each GPU.
- Load DeepSeek MoE 16B in 8.54 GiB on gfx90a,
  gfx1100, and gfx1201.
- Generate coherent output on all three targets.
- Initial native-kernel sandbox run skipped: uv
  was unavailable.
- Original two-patch series passed 14 focused
  tests on each benchmark host.
- Validate native GEMM on gfx90a and gfx1201.
- Rebuild that series on Felippe and Nicki.
- Run the complete fitting-model matrix with it.
- DeepSeek W4A8 throughput rose 9.2% on gfx1100,
  15.9% on gfx90a, and 29.5% on gfx1201.
- Repeated gfx1201 Qwen3.5 W8A8 A/B favored AITER:
  123.05 versus Triton's 120.57/120.61 tok/s.
- Omit the gfx1201 W8A8 routing change.

Tools used:
- GPT-5.6 Sol: coding agent
- Codex: GPT-6

Signed-off-by: Mika Laitio <mika.laitio@amd.com>

